Alumina ceramics according to the content of Al2O3 is divided into 99 porcelain, 95 porcelain, 92 porcelain and other varieties, sometimes Al2O3 content in 80% or 75% is also classified as ordinary alumina ceramics series.
95, 92 alumina porcelain is mainly used for ceramic grinding body used in corrosion resistance, wear resistance parts;
The aluminum oxide powder will be prepared into powder materials according to different product requirements and different forming processes. If you want to make high purity alumina ceramics, in addition to the purity of alumina in 99.99%, it is necessary to ultrafine grinding and make its particle size distribution uniform.
In the process of dry pressing, the uniform distribution of powder particles is very important for mold filling, and the accuracy of filling quantity has a great influence on the dimensional accuracy control of alumina ceramic parts.
The technology of densifying the granular ceramic body and forming a solid material is called sintering.
