The most commonly used molding technology for alumina ceramics
This molding method of alumina slurry is usually water as a medium to add binder and degelling agent, after grinding and then exhaust, and finally into the gypsum mold body.
Dry pressing method: this forming technique is only used for workpiece with simple shape, internal thickness of more than 1mm and diameter and length of not more than 4:1. The method is divided into two kinds: single axial and two-way axial.
The maximum pressure of the press is 200Mpa, which can produce about 15-50 pieces of workpiece per minute. Because of the average pressure distribution of the stroke of the hydraulic press, the height of the workpiece will be different when the filling powder is different.
Therefore, the powder distribution is not uniform in the process of dry pressing, which is particularly important for filling, and has a great influence on the precise size control of the alumina ceramic parts manufactured.
