Indiana University of PA Data
Lincoln University is one of Pennsylvania’s two Historically Black Colleges and Universities. It’s located just 45 minutes away from Lancaster.
Millersville University is Lancaster County’s public 4 year college. McCaskey grads attending the college can take advantage of a special scholarship through Lancaster Partnership Program.
Northampton is unique among community colleges as they offer a limited amount of on campus housing. They are an open access institution meaning that anyone who applies is automatically accepted.
PA College of Health Sciences is located just 10 minutes from McCaskey High School. The school focused on health careers with a variety of different degree and certificate options.
Pennsylvania College of Technology is a public college located in Williamsport, Pennsylvania. The college offers an impressive range of 2 and 4 year programs with a focus on applied technology.
West Chester University is one of Pennsylvania’s system of 4 year public universities.
Graduation Rate:73%
Widener University is a private university located in Chester, Pennsylvania with an additional campus in Harrisburg.
York College is a private college in York, Pennsylvania. It offers over 50 different majors on campus.
