Emphasis is on passive components and solid-state devices; digital circuits; optoelectronic devices; operational amplifiers; audio and RF amplifiers; oscillators; power supplies; and AM, FM, and PCM modulators. Knowledge is acquired through theoretical instruction, experimentation, and hands-on activities.
Instruction consists of core course content with clinical experiences in one or two health-related occupations. The core curriculum consists of the introduction of health careers, basic anatomy, and physiology, medical terminology, legal and ethical aspects of healthcare, and communications.
