SDoL is lead by a board of nine directors who are each elected to a four-year term of office. The board establishes policy, allocates resources and levies taxes and provides strategic direction.
A graduate of Coatesville Area High School, she has an associate’s degree in accounting from the Consolidated School of Business and studied psychology at Lincoln University. She lives in Lancaster with her husband and child, who is a student at McCaskey High School.
Dr. Gallagher was elected to the board in November 2015. She is a Research Oceanographer at Franklin and Marshall College and the proud mother of two recent McCaskey graduates.
She has a history as an educator, public health official and been active in many community service organizations. Her children attended the School District of Lancaster.
Luis Morales was appointed to fill a vacancy on the board in 2020. He is employed by Community Action Partnership and is a McCaskey graduate.
Our students: ready to take the next step
Regardless of whether a student goes on to college, the military, or the workforce, we want students to leave McCaskey prepared for their next step. We invest in our students’ readiness through a comprehensive K-12 college and career readiness curriculum, rigorous courses, and the opportunity to take college classes at no cost.
