Staff Protocols We need to be vigilant to isolate COVID-19 cases.
Due to individual privacy rights, we cannot divulge medical diagnoses of students or staff. However, if a COVID-19 diagnosis affects the public operations of a school or office in our district, we will notify all individuals and families who are impacted.
If individuals in our school system test positive, we will conduct contact tracing to identify people at risk of exposure and will notify the parents of students deemed in “close contact” with those individuals. Unvaccinated contacts will be required to quarantine for 10 days after exposure.
Also, unvaccinated students will not be required to quarantine if they are properly wearing a face covering, over the nose down to the chin.
To support contact tracing, we will again do vigilant contact monitoring, including all visitors to our buildings this year.
While families and employees monitor their own health, our school nurses will closely watch the data on student health trends. School nurses will continue to provide mandated health services including care of ill and injured students daily.
In an abundance of caution, students who displayed symptoms of communicable disease may only return to school only if:
they have been fever-free for 24+ hours without fever-reducing medications;
OR they present a note from a medical provider showing their symptoms are not related to COVID-19.
Note: These protocols refer to symptoms of any illness. We will follow much more rigorous guidelines if students (or staff) test positive for COVID-19.
The Full Circle Learning Program is a family-centered learning option that builds on the benefits and strengths of both traditional school and virtual learning. It allows students to form community as part of a class, participate in onsite learning and support, and engage in lessons that were planned and developed using the School District of Lancaster curriculum.
Full Circle Learning students will attend school in person four days per week, from 8:45 a.m. to 1 p.m. Each day, teachers will teach English, math, science and social studies and provide time for asynchronous practice, remediation, and/or acceleration, as well as personalized intervention provided by the classroom teacher or classroom aide.
Since two teachers will be planning lessons and instructing two classrooms of students, they will collaborate closely. This level of collaboration will give teaching teams broader insights into individual student needs, develop their instructional skills faster, and improve accountability for outcomes.
Any student entering kindergarten through third grade in the School District of Lancaster is eligible to apply for space in Full Circle Learning. Enrollment will be determined by random lottery to reflect the key demographics of the district.
Join our Full Circle Learning interest list to learn more about the program. We will continue to accept applications through most of the school year and you will be notified should your child be chosen to attend.
