News - 6 Bathroom Remodel Ideas That Add Value to Your Home
Since safety is important in the bathroom, consider adding textured tiles that prevent slips and falls.Additional grout helps fight mold, moisture and stains.
Eco-friendly or low-flow toilets help conserve water.If you’re looking for ways to help protect the environment and beautify your space, replace an older model.A low-flow toilet saves water (and money) every time you flush.
Mold and mildew are the bane of every bathroom.Consider adding windows or ventilation systems to help remove moisture.
If you don’t already have a bathroom fan, consider adding one.Fans will help prevent mold and mildew while significantly improving air quality.Unlike windows you might want to keep closed, you can run a bathroom ventilator year-round.
To facilitate the organization of the bathroom, combine open and closed storage spaces.This allows you to put away frequently used items like toiletries while displaying houseplants and gadgets.The closed door also conveniently hides hygiene products, plungers and clothing.For small storage updates, combine baskets and bins to separate dressers and cabinets.
Consider the scale of bathroom accessories when remodeling.For example, adding a basic round mirror to a small bathroom might create the illusion of a large space, but a chunky frame might make the room feel claustrophobic.The goal is to make the bathroom feel light and airy, not crowded.
Keep in mind that while there are many options for remodeling a bathroom, the most important thing to remember is how it will make you feel to be in the space every day (multiple times a day).If you plan to flip a guest bathroom or powder room on the first floor, channel the mood you want your guests to be in when they leave.This might mean setting aside your favorite color or trend in favor of a more universally appealing look.
