As users of Sure Start Services you will hopefully be aware that the Council has been dealing with budget reductions and over the last nine months there has been a review of services supporting families in the city.
The changes will take effect from Monday 1st June 2015.
The main change is that we have developed a Community Family Hub that covers the parts of the city shown in the shaded area below:
• Intensive Family Support for families with children up to age 18
• Services wrapped around families, delivered through buildings and in family homes
and What services can my family attend if we live outside the Community Family Hub area?
Many of the services you may use such as health visiting, midwifery, parent and toddler groups and childcare are not directly affected by the reduction in Council budgets; therefore access to those services is not affected by where you live.
We plan to keep all the buildings currently used by Sure Start open; however the variety of services and activities provided at individual sites may change.
They are regularly updated on the Sure Start Children’s Centre website and available in centres.
How will I get to know how the planned changes may affect me?
• Ensure that from Tuesday 7th April Sure Start staff in our centres are able to either answer your question directly or know where to get the answer.
• Write directly to those parents who have been using services during April 2014-March 2015 and who live outside the new Community Family Hub area.
Letters will be sent from week beginning April 7th.
• Provide information on the website from 11th May which will show the services you can access based on where you live using a new membership system.
