Your Personal Profile is an introductory paragraph that highlights all of your most important skills and knowledge.
Experience in preparing food and serving meals and refreshments to children
If this is your first post, then it is strongly advised that you include any experience and or transferable skills that you have. For example child minding, any unpaid child care work or babysitting,.
Also include experience gained as part of any courses you have undertaken.
What You Should NOT include on your Child CareAssistant CV
Of course you should be prepared to answer questions that may be considered personal. However, this can be addressed verbally, in a pre-interview meeting or at interview.
Your full address– it’s not needed at this stage. All that should be required is a location.
A photograph– Employers should only be interested in what skills and knowledge you can bring to their school. They should not make decisions on the basis of how you look.
