How To Turn Your Passion Into A Career You Love In 2021 - The Personal Development Cafe
1 Can You Really Turn Your Passion Into A Career?
With the number of people working from home increasing, one question that many people are asking is “How can you turn your passion into a career?”
So as thousands of qualified people compete for those highly sought after available jobs, this means that job search stressis rising.
One result of this mind shift is that more and more people are considering turning a passion or hobby into a career.
The simple answer is that yes you can turn your passion into a career.
The other 80%are ‘first-generation rich’. In other words they started from nothing and made their wealth.
As the famous Confucius quote says, “Work on what makes you happy, and you would never have to work in a single day for your entire life”.
According to research, at least 85% of the working-classworldwide hate their jobs. Many employees are simply in jobs for two main reasons: security and a paycheck.
These examples of amazing success don’t happen every day.
Let’s face it, pursuing your dreams can mean leaving your comfort zone and trying to take on tasks and responsibilities that you may have little knowledge about.
Yes, you have to be realistic. There are numerous failures on first business start ups, therefore many people end up discouraged and quickly give up as things go from fun to frustration.
It means that you have to really want to make a success of your idea. Allow yourself time to build and grow your business.
Here are some steps you need to keep in mind if you believe you can successfully turn your passion into a career.
Think in terms of things that really excite you and fill you with enthusiasm. Or activities that inspire you and give you the purpose to live.
The key is to understand that any activity that you enjoy doing can be transformed into a successful full-time career.
A great example of this is Footprints Through The Lens photography.
If you are thinking about a career in writing because you love playing around with words, are there other specific skills that could enhance your success?
Using all 3 skills you could capture and develop great visuals and at the same time promote them in your social media accounts as a way of marketing.
So, your task is to figure out your secret ingredients of success that would be made up of different sets of skills and experiences that are specific to you.
With the advancement in today’s technology, there are a myriad of ways to build your circle and reach out to people who would be of value to you.
For instance, if you enjoy teaching, you need to have a clear idea of ways you can reach institutions that would require your services.
Teaching abroad may be a viable option you are considering and can also reduce competition for your services. This is crucial when you want your career to flourish in the long run.
If you love blogging, then you can use social media platforms. Once people are familiar with your work and get value from it, you can now focus on building your portfolio for prospective clients.
Just like in any other ordinary job. These adjustments present one important aspect: identifying what works for you and what does not.
Always remember, change is as good as rest.
Taking a plunge in a field with low demand is like diving into the deep end of a pool: It is very dangerous. However; you may offer a specific skill or service that could be just what people are crying out for.
Always make sure you carefully and objectively assess the demand. Conduct market research to find out if your services are in demand.
This is one area where many people fail. Before you embark on pursuing your dreams, it is imperative that you must have honed your skills first.
For example, if you love teaching, you could start by volunteering in your local schools.
It takes time and adequate preparations before turning skills into a career. Sharpening your skills and building confidence should be your initial goals.
Chances are, if you do not enjoy doing it for free, you may not enjoy doing it for money either.
Turning your passion into a career is not an easy journey. You have to be prepared for setbacks, disappointment and frustrations.
Turning your passion into a career can be done.
If you want proof that you can turn your passion into a career, here’s an amazing fact – more than 4 of the world’s richest peopledid not inherit their wealth, but earned it from businesses they had started.
Now is the time to think creatively and broadly. Some great suggestions here.
The future is uncertain right now, so we have no time to waste dwelling on how great things were before the pandemic.
While many people are in limbo during this pandemic, it could be the perfect time to re-assess or re-evaluate the possibilities going forward.
You don’t have to put all your eggs into one basket. Indeed being ‘stuck at home’ can allow you to start small and test the waters.
