Another intrepid explorer, John Thistle captain of the expedition ship, did not hesitate to approach the lake itself to see if what he had seen was real or an optical effect. When he approached he got a great surprise and did not hesitate to take a water sample from Lake Hillier to show it to the rest of your companions.
