In Indonesia there is a place known as the island of Flores where the Kelimutu volcano, which has three lakes whose waters change color: from turquoise to red through dark blue and brown. Incredible true?
Despite being an active volcano, the last Kelimutu eruption was in 1968. At the end of the XNUMXth century, its environment was declared a national park in Indonesia.
Located on the border between Tanzania and Kenya, Lake Natron It is a landlocked saltwater lake above the Great Rift Valley. Due to the sodium carbonate and other mineral compounds that flow into the lake from the surrounding mountains, its alkaline waters have an incredible pH of 10.5 due to the sodium carbonate and other mineral compounds.
But regarding its external appearance, this lagoon acquires a unique red or pink color, sometimes even orange in the lower areas, due to the microorganisms that live in the crust created by alkaline salt. Amazing!
