On the day of the expedition to Middle Island, Flinders decided to ascend to the highest peak so that he could scan the surroundings. It was then that he was amazed at that incredible image that appeared before his eyes: that of a huge bright pink lake surrounded by sand and jungle.
It is the great mystery of Lake Hillier that No one has been able to reveal 100% is the reason why its waters are pink. Most researchers think that the pond has this hue because of the bacteria that are in the crust of the salt.
