Since its introduction, the robot vacuum cleaner has been a popular product, so the emergence of the robot mop is only a matter of time. These automatic cleaning gadgets are perfect for people with hard floors because they can wipe off dirt and grime without you having to lift the bucket.
First of all, you need to decide whether you need a model for mopping the floor alone or a combined device that can also vacuum. It is also important to consider the size of your home and compare it to the range of the mop-some models can easily clean more than 2,000 square feet, while others are more suitable for use in just one room.
I personally tested some robotic mops, so I use my own experience using these cleaning tools to guide the product selection in this article. I look for models that provide longer runtimes and are easy to use, prioritizing mops that require the least effort from users.
Bissell SpinWave integrates vacuum wet mopping, providing excellent running time and multiple advanced functions to make your life easier. It has a two-tank system-one for vacuuming and one for mopping-you can replace it according to your own cleaning method, and the robot can run for more than 130 minutes after each charge.
The Roborock S6 can mop up to 1,610 square feet on a single water tank, which is very suitable for large families, and when vacuuming, it will automatically increase the suction power when it senses the carpet. The robot can be controlled by Siri and Alexa, and you can set an automatic cleaning plan through the device’s app.
Many robotic vacuum cleaners simply wipe wet pads on the floor to remove dust and dirt, but ILIFE Shinebot W400s actually use a scrubbing action to leave your home. It has a four-stage cleaning system that can spray water, use a microfiber roller to scrub, suck out dirty water, and wipe away the residue with a rubber scraper.
This high-end model can vacuum and mop, and is equipped with a HEPA filter that efficiently filters dust and dust. It has a large 1.3 gallon water tank that can mop more than 2,000 square feet at a time, and its dual mop head rotates at high speed for thorough cleaning.
Braava 240 can be placed in small spaces, such as behind the sink base and around the toilet, and it will automatically select the correct cleaning method based on the type of mat you install. You can eject the cleaning pad by pressing a button, so you don’t have to deal with the dirt, and if you want, you can also set an invisible border to keep the mop in one area.
Jetbot has a unique shape that can rotate and easily reach the edge of your home when cleaning. You can set it to a variety of different cleaning modes, including edge, focus, auto, etc.
This robot mop uses a precision sprayer to spray water onto your floor and clean it with the brand’s wet mop pad. If the battery is low, it will automatically return to its base and recharge, and you can give it commands through a compatible voice assistant.
You don’t have to worry about DEEBOT U2 dying in the middle of the floor, because this sweeping robot and mopping robot will automatically return to its docking station when the battery is low. The robot can run for up to 110 minutes on a single charge.
